  "summary_en": "Philippine House Bill 4797, the \"Drone-Free Jails Act\", would prohibit operating drones within 100 meters of jail facilities, except with a CAAP permit and jail authority consent. It sets fines and imprisonment, requires forfeited drones to be turned over to CAAP, and tells CAAP to publish no-drone-zone notices.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Unlawful to operate UAVs/drones within 100 m of jail facilities for any purpose.",
   "Exception for emergencies with a CAAP permit and jail authority consent, or custodial security purposes.",
   "Penalty: fine of P50,000–P200,000 and/or one year imprisonment.",
   "Confiscated drones turned over to CAAP within 15 days after the case ends.",
   "CAAP must publish and update no-drone-zone restrictions."
  ],
